, and to large mining companies outside the U.S. These customers want to work with AES due to our track record of providing customized solutions that best serve their specific needs and delivering our projects on time and on budget.","zh":null}],"markets":[{"en":"The segment reporting structure uses the Company's management reporting structure as its foundation to reflect how the Company manages the businesses internally and is mainly organized by technology.","zh":null},{"en":"We are organized into four technology-oriented SBUs: Renewables (solar, wind, energy storage, and hydro generation facilities); Utilities (AES Indiana, AES Ohio, and AES El Salvador regulated utilities and their generation facilities); Energy Infrastructure (natural gas, LNG, coal, pet coke, diesel, and oil generation facilities); and New Energy Technologies (investments in Fluence, Maximo and other new and innovative energy technology businesses) — which are led by our SBU Presidents.","zh":null}],"customers":[{"en":"We sell to a wide variety of customers. No individual customer accounted for 10% or more of our 2025 total revenue. In our generation business, we own and/or operate power plants to sell power to wholesale customers such as utilities and other intermediaries, as well as to large corporations. Our utilities sell to end-user customers in the residential, commercial, industrial, and governmental sectors in a defined service area.","zh":null},{"en":"At AES, our people are instrumental to helping us meet the world's energy needs. Supporting our people is a foundational value for AES. Our actions are grounded in the shared values that shape AES' culture: Safety First, Highest Standards, and All Together. The AES Corporation is led and managed by our Chief Executive Officer and the Global Leadership Team with the guidance and oversight of our Board of Directors. Governance and standards for AES people are guided by the Chief Human Resources Officer, with input from members of the Global Leadership Team.","zh":null}],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Energy Infrastructure","val":5402000000,"zh":"Energy Infrastructure"},{"name":"Utilities","val":4122000000,"zh":"Utilities"},{"name":"Renewables","val":2913000000,"zh":"Renewables"},{"name":"AES Andes","val":900000000,"zh":"AES Andes"},{"name":"New Energy Technologies","val":1000000,"zh":"New Energy Technologies"}],"total":12233000000},"prod":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Electricity Generation","val":8195000000,"zh":"Electricity Generation"},{"name":"Nonregulatedrevenue","val":8195000000,"zh":"Nonregulatedrevenue"},{"name":"Electric Distribution","val":4038000000,"zh":"Electric Distribution"},{"name":"Regulated Revenue","val":4038000000,"zh":"Regulated Revenue"}],"total":12233000000},"geo":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Total Non Us","val":7177000000,"zh":"Total Non Us"},{"name":"US","val":5056000000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"CL","val":1516000000,"zh":"CL"},{"name":"DO","val":1363000000,"zh":"DO"},{"name":"SV","val":1086000000,"zh":"SV"},{"name":"MX","val":760000000,"zh":"墨西哥"},{"name":"BG","val":687000000,"zh":"BG"},{"name":"PA","val":649000000,"zh":"PA"},{"name":"CO","val":422000000,"zh":"CO"},{"name":"PR","val":404000000,"zh":"PR"}],"total":12233000000}},"peers":["EIX","CNP","CMS","ETR","AEP"]}}